# ReadPST/LibPST 0.6.76 Corresponding Source

This directory is the Corresponding Source companion for the ReadPST sidecars
bundled with PST QuickView. It contains the exact authoritative source archive,
the local patch, and the build and verification material used for the bundled
macOS x86_64 and arm64 binaries.

- Component: ReadPST/LibPST 0.6.76
- Component license: GPL-2.0-or-later
- Authoritative source: https://www.five-ten-sg.com/libpst/packages/libpst-0.6.76.tar.gz
- Source SHA-256: `3d291beebbdb48d2b934608bc06195b641da63d2a8f5e0d386f2e9d6d05a0b42`
- Deployment targets: x86_64 macOS 10.13; arm64 macOS 11.0
- Public companion location: @PUBLIC_DOWNLOAD_LOCATION@

`LICENSE` is the unmodified GNU GPL version 2 text. The upstream archive also
retains its own license, author, copyright, and generated-build notices.
`COPYRIGHT_NOTICES.md` summarizes the principal upstream notices without
replacing the notices in the archive.

## Local modification

`patches/0001-disable-msg-output.patch` disables ReadPST's optional `.msg`
writer. PST QuickView invokes ReadPST only for EML extraction, so this removes
the libgsf/glib requirement from the bundled command-line tool. No other local
source patches are applied.

## Rebuild

Follow `build/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md`. The exact build script validates the
source and patch hashes, enforces the recorded Apple clang and SDK versions,
builds both architecture slices, creates the universal binary, checks the
version and architecture, rejects non-system dynamic libraries, and stages the
outputs only after every check succeeds.

`DEPLOYMENT_TARGETS.txt` records the minimum for each standalone binary and
each universal slice. The universal binary preserves different minimums per
slice; it does not have one global deployment target.

`SIDECAR_SHA256.txt` identifies the exact sidecars for which this companion was
prepared. `MANIFEST.sha256` covers every companion file except the manifest
itself. The deterministic companion archive is accompanied by its own `.sha256`
file outside this directory.

This source companion does not contain PST QuickView binaries, app bundles,
DMGs, message files, signing material, private logs, or Git metadata.
